                    "An easement is a right to use a defined area for a defined purpose. The dominant estate benefits from the right, while the servient estate carries the burden. An appurtenant easement generally runs with the land and can matter to a successor if the instrument and local law support that result; an easement in gross benefits a person or entity identified in the document. The written instrument, the location shown on a plat, and the actual route should be reviewed together. A verbal permission from a current neighbor may not bind successors, and a recorded right may still be narrow, expired, relocated, or subject to conditions that are easy to overlook.",
