                    "Zoning assigns uses and development standards to land, but a parcel’s legal right to build is also shaped by private restrictions, easements, road rules, environmental requirements, and the jurisdiction’s permitting process. Start by identifying the controlling municipality or county, the zoning district, any overlay district, and the comprehensive plan. Confirm whether the proposed project needs a conditional-use permit, rezoning, variance, subdivision approval, or special exception. A use may be listed as permitted while dimensional, access, or environmental conditions still prevent the planned layout. Treat a parcel description from a listing as a lead, not as a development approval.",
